B.aiO=new A.yQ("cisco","Cisco (Catalyst / Aironet / IW, plus Meraki CW)","High","Cisco encodes position by position, and the trailing letter after the dash is the regulatory domain. Do not confuse that trailing E (a domain) with the antenna E.",B.aTC,"C9130AXI-B",B.aJO,"Catalyst 9130, 802.11ax, internal antennas, US-class regulatory domain.","Confidence: High. Sourced from the Catalyst 9130AX datasheet, the Getting Started Guide, the 9100 FAQ, and reseller SKU listings corroborating the internal/external and domain split. The trailing-letter-equals-domain rule is the one users most often misread; it is called out explicitly above.",null,B.o)
