B.DD=s(["You read these codes on every outdoor and industrial AP, antenna, PoE injector, and enclosure spec sheet. The injector zip-tied under an eave is the classic weak install. Spec the enclosure to the actual hazard, and translate NEMA to IP (or back) so you can compare US and international gear on the same terms.","A rating describes a lab test, not a guarantee. Verify the manufacturer's stated rating on the real spec sheet (for IP68, the stated depth and time), and match it to the real hazard at the mount point."],t.s)
B.bYR=new A.pO("A handful of controls decide what the trace shows. Set them wrong and you hide the very thing you are hunting.",null)
B.bTh=new A.jI("Span. ","The frequency range displayed, between a start and stop. Wide span gives a whole-band overview; narrow span zooms in on one signal.")
B.bT2=new A.jI("RBW (resolution bandwidth). ","The narrowest frequency difference the analyzer can separate. A narrower RBW separates closely spaced signals and lowers the noise floor, revealing weaker signals, but it slows the sweep.")
B.bSV=new A.jI("VBW (video bandwidth). ","A post-detection filter that smooths the displayed trace so a noisy signal is easier to read. It changes only the displayed trace, not the underlying signal.")
B.bT_=new A.jI("Reference level. ","The amplitude at the top of the display. It sets the analyzer\u2019s gain and attenuation so strong signals are not clipped and weak ones are not buried.")
B.bTe=new A.jI("Amplitude scale (dBm). ","The vertical axis, a logarithmic power scale in decibels relative to one milliwatt. More negative means weaker.")
B.bST=new A.jI("Detectors. ","How each displayed point is derived from the many samples behind it. Peak catches bursts; average or RMS gives true power for noise-like signals; sample takes one instantaneous value. The detector changes what the trace means.")
B.bSY=new A.jI("Max-hold and averaging. ","Trace-processing modes. Max-hold keeps the highest value ever seen at each frequency; averaging smooths toward the mean. More on these under Comparing captures.")
B.aDi=s([B.bTh,B.bT2,B.bSV,B.bT_,B.bTe,B.bST,B.bSY],t.G1)
B.bTk=new A.QD(B.aDi,!1,null)
B.bVi=new A.avb(null)
